  "name": "Node.js",
  "description": "Node.js is a high-performance, asynchronous event-driven JavaScript runtime built on Chrome's V8 engine and the libuv platform abstraction layer. It provides a non-blocking I/O model designed for scalable network applications, exposing low-level system primitives through a comprehensive standard library. The architecture supports both CommonJS and ECMAScript modules, multi-threaded execution via Worker Threads, and high-efficiency native extensibility through the Node-API.",
